#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 29.1: Credential landing page - Certificate
#################################################################

cred:Req_29_1_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Certificate landing page: actions, status, and navigation eligibility" ;
    sd:statement "(No user-story stem given in the FDD for this item — it is the feature's baseline acceptance criteria, not phrased as a story.) The system displays actions such as Apply/Renew, Add Endorsement, Print Certificate, and access to certification guidance documents; displays each certificate's status (Valid, Expired, Nullified, Revoked, Suspended); and allows navigation to application flows when available based on eligibility." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Landing page action set as defined in the main spec; certificate status shown per certificate; navigation to application flows gated by eligibility." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials, cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate ;
    sd:notes "Status vocabulary (Valid/Expired/Nullified/Revoked/Suspended) is an exact match to cred:CredState_Valid/Expired/Nullified/Revoked/Suspended. Op_GetEducatorCredentials's own EducatorCredentialSummary projection (all credentials+endorsements grouped by educator) is the natural backing call. Comment thread 181233542/6381586 (Punniyamoorthy: 'this landing page is more like Dashboard... I do not see any other story for other functionality like dashboard' / Caswell, agreeing the global Citizen Dashboard is broader but this FDD is deliberately scoped to certificate-related aspects only) is the same landing-page-vs-Dashboard overlap the FDD 11/16 pass already surfaced for dash:DashboardsContext (Req_11_7 there) — resolved amicably in-thread, not a new gap, so not re-raised as its own Annotation here." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Display eligible certificate actions (MTTC/PKS-aware)" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want the system to show only the certificate actions I am eligible for, so that I do not attempt actions that I cannot perform." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Apply/Renew eligibility per certificate-type prerequisites; Apply/Renew disabled/hidden when Needs Responses = Y; Add Endorsement NOT disabled for lack of MTTC score alone (not all endorsements require a test); on attempting to add a specific endorsement, dynamically verify whether it requires MTTC or a Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS) test, and require a passing score not older than 5 years; block adding that endorsement with an error if no valid passing score is on file; Print Certificate disabled if no valid certificate exists." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AssessmentResultValidity, cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation ;
    sd:notes "5-year validity window is an exact match to Rule_AssessmentResultValidity. Per-endorsement dynamic test-requirement check (some require none) matches Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's AND/OR-configurable requirement model. Genuine new detail: comment 2095209523/1225736752 (Dontje: 'some endorsements require a Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS) test' / 'Added') introduced PKS as a SECOND named test type alongside MTTC mid-review — nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl's AssessmentDefinition/AssessmentResult model names PKS specifically (nor does it need to, if PKS is just another configured AssessmentDefinition instance — but that's an assumption, not confirmed anywhere). See Question_PksAssessmentTypeUnconfirmed below. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating is a distinct, still-unmodeled flag — see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled (shared with several other stories below)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Display pending applications, with conditional delete" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to view my pending certificate applications, so that I can track the status of applications that have not yet been processed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display all applications in Submitted or Pending statuses, using main-workflow-consistent status text (flow diagrams show routing to OPPS, EPP, or Alternate Route Providers depending on type); show a Delete option only while Submitted; prevent deletion once routing has begun (OPPS/EPP/ARP involvement)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListApplications, cred:Op_DeleteApplication, cred:AppState_Submitted ;
    sd:notes "Good direct match on the Submitted-only delete gate (Op_DeleteApplication's own summary is literally 'Delete draft application', and cred:AppState_Submitted is a real, early, non-terminal state). 'OPPS' (undefined acronym here — likely 'Office of Professional Preparation Services' or similar) and 'Alternate Route Providers' as named routing destinations don't correspond to any modeled concept in credentialing-domain.ttl beyond the generic worklist/manual-review routing (Rule_ManualReviewTriggering) — minor terminology gap, not raised as its own Annotation given how minor it is." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.4" ;
    sd:title "Navigate to Apply/Renew" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to select Apply/Renew from my landing page, so that I can begin a new credential application or renewal." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display eligible certificates to apply for/renew per eligibility flows (e.g. Interim -> Standard, Provisional -> Professional); show an error if ineligible; prevent starting when Needs Responses = Y or PPR indicates actionable restrictions." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance, cred:Op_SubmitApplication, cred:Op_SubmitRenewal, cred:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication, cred:Seq_RenewCredential ;
    sd:notes "PPR-actionable gating matches Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance well (Blocked/Hold semantics). Interim->Standard / Provisional->Professional progression path terminology matches cred:ProgressToProfessional (an EndorsementDefinition field, per credentialing-domain.ttl line ~310) only loosely — that field is endorsement-scoped, not a certificate-level state-machine transition; a genuine, if minor, terminology/granularity gap. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating: see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.5" ;
    sd:title "Navigate to Add Endorsement" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to select Add Endorsement from my landing page, so that I can add new endorsements to my existing certificates." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display available endorsements for the certificate type (flow diagrams show validation based on MTTC test scores, endorsement level, and grade band rules); display static text that MTTC scores must be verified for approval; show an error if prerequisites for endorsement addition aren't met." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition, cred:Op_ListEndorsementApplications, cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation ;
    sd:notes "Direct match; grade-band filtering matches cred:GradeBandRange on EndorsementDefinitionAggregate." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.6" ;
    sd:title "Navigate to Print Certificate" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to print my certificate, so that I can produce an official version for my employer or personal records." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display Print Certificate for any valid certificate; generate a PDF containing certificate type, endorsements, issue date and expiration date (or blank for revoked/nullified/suspended per main spec); allow download or printing." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_PrintCredential, cred:Seq_PrintCertificate, cred:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration ;
    sd:notes "CITATION VERIFIED: this story is one of Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration's two cited sources for the blank-date-on-Revoked/Nullified/Suspended rendering rule, and it does say almost exactly that ('Issue date and expiration date (or blank for revoked/nullified/suspended per main spec)') — accurate citation, no correction needed. Comment 1070770097 (Dontje: 'your attachment is a sample ITC but the citizen user will be able to print their certificate(s) regardless of type') confirms Print Certificate isn't type-restricted, consistent with Op_PrintCredential's own general shape." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.7" ;
    sd:title "Display certificate guidance documents" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to access certificate-related guidance documents from my landing page, so that I can understand requirements and processes." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display a link/section for guidance documents; open in a new tab or viewer; ensure documents reflect current certificate/endorsement rules." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Perm_GuidanceView ;
    sd:notes "Same structural gap the FDD 11/16 pass already found for this same permission (Req_11_2_1/11_2_2 there): cred:Perm_GuidanceView exists but has no backing ApiOperation/Sequence anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl in mied-v3 either — this is carried-forward, not newly introduced. Not re-raised as its own Annotation; folded into the existing known gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.8" ;
    sd:title "Persistent certificate dashboard state" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want the system to remember my certificate landing page preferences, so my view is consistent each time I return." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Store dashboard preferences tied to the user profile; display the user's preferred section/widget arrangement on return; preferences persist across sessions and devices." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl models a per-user dashboard-preference concept, and per the comment-thread resolution on 29.1.1 (181233542/6381586) this kind of cross-cutting dashboard/widget behavior is explicitly the Dashboards capability's territory (dash:DashboardsContext — a stub-only context in this project, same as the FDD 11/16 pass found for its own Req_11_7). Genuine coverage gap from Credentialing's own graph, but out-of-scope in the same sense Req_11_7 was — see the coverage-gap Annotation below rather than treating it as a Credentialing-side build item." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Persistent per-user dashboard/widget-arrangement state (29.1.8) belongs to the Dashboards capability (dash:DashboardsContext), consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pass's Req_11_7 treated the same kind of cross-cutting dashboard concern for Credentialing's own landing-page content. Not a Credentialing-side build item." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_1_8 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.9" ;
    sd:title "Display certificate and endorsement details" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to view details for each certificate and its endorsements, so that I understand what I hold and what I can apply for." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display certificate type, status, validity dates, and endorsements; visually distinguish revoked/suspended/nullified certificates (dates may be blank); display endorsements and their grade bands." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials, cred:Op_GetCredential, cred:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration, cred:AssociatedEndorsements ;
    sd:notes "CITATION VERIFIED: this is Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration's second cited source for the blank-date rule ('The system visually distinguishes revoked, suspended, or nullified certificates (as their dates may be blank)') — accurate, consistent wording with 29.1.6. Grade-band display matches cred:GradeBandRange (via cred:AssociatedEndorsements on IssuedCredentialAggregate)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_1_10 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.1.10" ;
    sd:title "Display system alerts related to credentialing" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want to see alerts related to my certifications, so that I am aware of required updates or incomplete prerequisites." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display alerts for: expiring certificates, insufficient professional learning hours, missing MTTC scores, PPR/Needs Responses status blocking actions. Alerts link to the appropriate actions/pages." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no alert/notification model of any kind exists in credentialing-domain.ttl or credentialing-api.ttl — this is explicitly Alerts & Communications (Business Specification #6) territory per the Dependencies section's own 'email notification... will be defined in Alerts and Communications (6)' line, matching how the FDD 11/16 pass's Req_11_6/16_3 treated the same deferral. Out-of-scope, not a coverage gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Alert/notification generation and display (29.1.10) is owned by Business Specification #6 (Alerts and Communications) per this FDD's own Dependencies section, consistent with comm:CommunicationsContext already existing as a stub subscribing to Credentialing's own events." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_1_10 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 29.2: All Types (generic application flow)
#################################################################

cred:Req_29_2_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.1" ;
    sd:title "View eligible certificate types to Apply/Renew" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to view a list of all certificate types for which I am eligible to Apply/Renew, so that I can easily initiate the correct application process." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Evaluate eligibility per Credentialing-Administrator-defined prerequisites; display only eligible certificate types (Teaching, ITC, School Counselor, School Administrator, School Psychologist, School Social Worker); hide ineligible types, including those ineligible due to Needs Responses = Y or PPR restrictions; navigate into the appropriate flow on selection." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitApplication, cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance ;
    sd:notes "Comment thread 2062160207 ('seems already covered in 29.1.4') -> 2092676098 ('you are correct, user story has been removed') indicates an earlier, more duplicative draft of this story was trimmed during review; the surviving 29.2.1 text is scoped distinctly enough from 29.1.4 (list-of-types vs. navigate-to-flow) that it's kept as its own Requirement here. 'Needs Responses = Y' gating: see Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Begin the appropriate application flow per certificate type" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want the system to begin the appropriate application flow when I select a certificate type, so that I can proceed through the required questions and validations." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Load the certificate-type-specific flow; display type-specific question sets per Business Rule Management; adjust question sets across Teaching/ITC/Counselor/Administrator/Psychologist/Social Worker; block progress on unanswered required questions; move to upload/validation steps on completion." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication, cred:CredentialDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:notes "Per-certificate-type dynamic question sets aren't modeled as a distinct configuration concept in credentialing-domain.ttl beyond CredentialDefinition's general eligibility-rule configurability — partial match, not a hard gap (this is squarely the kind of 'Business Rule Management' decision-tree content credentialing-technical-design.ttl's own Question_ConfigurabilityModel already flags as unresolved)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.3" ;
    sd:title "Field-level and application-level validation for all certificate types" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform field-level and application-level validations during the application flow for all certificate types, so that incomplete or erroneous submissions are prevented and errors/warnings are displayed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Field-level validation on entry; application-level validation before submission; errors block submission until resolved; warnings allow submission but remain visible; all validation outcomes logged on the application record." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication, cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering ;
    sd:notes "Direct match for the block-on-error/warn-but-allow shape; 'all validation outcomes logged' as a discrete audit concept isn't explicitly modeled beyond IssuanceHistory's general audit-trail scope on the issued-credential side (not the in-flight application side) — minor gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.4" ;
    sd:title "Upload supporting documents for any certificate application" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want the ability to upload supporting documents for my application, so that I can provide necessary evidence for credentialing requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Upload fields per certificate type; accept only allowed file types; validate required-upload presence; block progress on missing required uploads; store uploaded documents with the application record." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload ;
    sd:notes "Unlike the FDD 11/16 pilot pass (which predated documents-api.ttl's real mied-v3 conversion and could only point at a placeholder docs:DocumentRetrievalOperation stub), mied-v3's documents-api.ttl now has a real docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload — a genuinely good match, not a stub-only reference. Per-certificate-type upload-field configuration (which uploads are required for which certificate type) still isn't modeled as a distinct concept anywhere, consistent with Credential Admin (11)'s general configurability scope." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.5" ;
    sd:title "Collect and process required fees via CEPAS" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I need to collect and process required fees for all certificate applications, utilizing CEPAS services, so that application costs are secured." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display fee amount for the selected certificate type; collect payment via the CEPAS payment service; prevent submission until payment succeeds; display an error on failed payment; log successful payment against the application record." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PaymentRequirement, pay:PaymentsContext ;
    sd:notes "WireframeAddendumC (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates the CEPAS-named payment error state described here. Credentialing's own Dependency on pay:PaymentsContext (event-subscription on PaymentCompletedEvent) matches the 'log successful payment' half; the CEPAS-specific integration detail (vs. a generic Payments-capability abstraction) lives in payments' own domain, not credentialing's, consistent with existing scope." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.6" ;
    sd:title "Real-time MTTC validation on endorsement selection" ;
    sd:statement "As a Citizen User, I want the system to validate my MTTC test completion when I select endorsements during an application, so that I know immediately if I am eligible to apply for that specific subject area." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Real-time check for a passing score tied to the endorsement's test code on selection; visual indicator next to the endorsement; block submission with an error if a Core-Subject endorsement requiring a test has no passing score; allow proceeding without a score if the endorsement requires none." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation, cred:Rule_AssessmentResultValidity ;
    sd:notes "Direct match, including the exception-handling branch for no-test-required endorsements. This story's explicit 'shall display an error message preventing the user from proceeding' (hard block at selection time, not after submission) is the SAME resolution the FDD 11/16 pass's Question_ManualReviewVsHardBlockForMttc already flagged as contradicting credentialing-domain.md's Rule_ManualReviewTriggering (which lists missing/failing assessment results as a MANUAL REVIEW trigger, not a submission-time hard block) — this FDD independently reinforces the hard-block reading a second time, strengthening that existing open contradiction rather than raising a new one." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.7" ;
    sd:title "Determine application status from Needs Responses flag" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must determine the status of the application based on the Needs Responses flag, so that applications proceed according to Professional Practices Review requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Check the Needs Responses flag on submission; prevent starting/renewing when Needs Responses = Y unless a rule explicitly allows continuation; continue normal processing when N; record the outcome in application metadata; display informational messaging." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: 'Needs Responses' as a distinct flag from ProfessionalPracticeStatus (Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold/Blocked) does not exist anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's CredentialApplication model, in mied-v3 exactly as in the FDD 11/16 pass's finding on this same gap (there, Req_11_4_1). See the consolidated Question_NeedsResponsesFlagNotModeled below (targets this Requirement plus 29.1.2/29.1.4/29.2.1/29.2.8/29.2.9, all of which independently reference the same still-unmodeled flag)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.8" ;
    sd:title "Route application to worklist based on PPR flag" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must route the application to the appropriate worklist(s) based on the Professional Practice Review (PPR) flag, so that staff review is initiated when necessary." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Check PPR flag for actionable status after submission; route to the required worklist if actionable; allow standard processing if not actionable; log routing decisions with timestamp and flag values; confirm submission and routing to the user." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance, cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering ;
    sd:notes "Core routing logic matches well. The discrete NAMED worklists with per-type search/filters that the FDD 11/16 pass's Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX already flagged as unmodeled UX aren't re-described here (this FDD doesn't itself describe worklist search screens), so not re-raised as a separate Annotation — same known gap, no new evidence either way." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.9" ;
    sd:title "Process/assign application by in-state vs. out-of-state" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must process or assign the application based on whether the applicant is In-state or Out-of-state, so that proper handling procedures are followed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Determine In-state/Out-of-state from data captured in the application flow; apply certificate-type-specific validation/routing rules; follow a specialized evaluation path for Out-of-state; log the determination; let it influence routing, document requirements, and processing logic." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: an applicant-level In-state/Out-of-state determination does not exist anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl. The only similarly-named field found is cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate's own 'OutOfState' ValueObject flag, but that describes special handling for an ENDORSEMENT TYPE, not an applicant's residency/application-routing status — a different concept with a confusingly similar name. Genuine coverage gap; see the coverage-gap Annotation below (grouped with Needs Responses since both are applicant/application-level flags absent from the same aggregate)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "'Needs Responses' (Y/N, distinct from ProfessionalPracticeStatus) and applicant-level In-state/Out-of-state are both referenced repeatedly across this FDD (Needs Responses: 29.1.2, 29.1.4, 29.2.1, 29.2.7, 29.2.8 all mention it; In-state/Out-of-state: 29.2.9 and the main Business Specifications section's per-certificate-type flow list) as gating/routing inputs on CredentialApplicationAggregate, but neither exists anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's application model. This is the SAME 'Needs Responses' gap the FDD 11/16 pass already surfaced (there, Req_11_4_1/Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance) — independently re-confirmed by a second, later FDD, which raises confidence this is a real, permanent field the domain model is missing, not a one-off FDD-specific quirk. In-state/Out-of-state is new to this pass; cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate's similarly-named 'OutOfState' field is a different, endorsement-type-scoped concept and should not be conflated with it." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_1_2, cred:Req_29_1_4, cred:Req_29_2_1, cred:Req_29_2_7, cred:Req_29_2_8, cred:Req_29_2_9 ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_2_10 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.2.10" ;
    sd:title "Submit application when complete" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to submit my application when all required information is complete, so that the credential review process can begin." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Block submission until all required fields/uploads/fees/validations succeed; create an application record with all inputs on submission; trigger Alerts & Communications alerts/emails; lock initial user-entered data from further editing; display confirmation and route as required." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitApplication, cred:Seq_SubmitNewCertificateApplication ;
    sd:notes "Direct match. 'Locks initial user-entered data from further editing' isn't an explicit invariant on CredentialApplicationAggregate today but is consistent with its state model (post-Submitted states don't describe a citizen-editable path back to Draft) — not raised as a separate gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 29.3: Certificates - Additional Endorsements
#################################################################

cred:Req_29_3_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.1" ;
    sd:title "Initiate additional endorsement request" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to initiate an additional endorsement request from my landing page, so that I can begin the process of adding an endorsement to my eligible certificate." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Verify the user holds an existing certificate eligible for endorsement addition; offer a certificate-type choice (Teacher or School Administrator) when more than one is eligible; disable/hide the action if none is eligible; navigate to the type-specific endorsement flow on confirmed eligibility; log initiation." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition, cred:Op_ListEndorsementApplications ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.2" ;
    sd:title "Verify certificate eligibility before allowing additional endorsement" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must verify that the existing certificate is eligible before allowing a citizen user to apply for an additional endorsement, so that application errors are minimized." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Confirm a valid, active certificate exists for endorsement addition; check Credential-Admin-defined eligibility rules (prerequisites, certificate type, status); prevent continuation with an informational message if ineligible; results determine which endorsement options display; log all eligibility checks and outcomes." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialDefinitionAggregate, cred:CredState_Valid ;
    sd:notes "No PPR/Needs-Responses check appears anywhere in this story's acceptance criteria — see this file's header note on Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's Feature-29.3 citation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.3" ;
    sd:title "Display eligible endorsements for Teacher certificates" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to see a list of available additional endorsements for Teacher certificates, so that I can select the specific endorsement I wish to add." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display available endorsements for a selected Teacher certificate; allow selecting an endorsement even before prerequisite verification (verification occurs on next step); log displayed options." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.4" ;
    sd:title "Display eligible endorsements for School Administrator certificates" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I must display the list of available additional endorsements for School Administrator certificates, so that the user can select the specific endorsement they wish to add." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display available endorsements for a selected School Administrator certificate; require an endorsement selection to proceed; log displayed endorsements." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.5" ;
    sd:title "Capture application inputs for additional endorsement" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to provide inputs required for the additional endorsement application, so that my submission meets the required criteria." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display all required/optional questions per Business Rule Management for the selected endorsement; block progress on incomplete required inputs; mark optional inputs; save all inputs to the endorsement application record." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.6" ;
    sd:title "Upload supporting documents for additional endorsement" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to upload documents when applying for an additional endorsement, so that I can support my application." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Upload fields per certificate type; block submission on missing/invalid required uploads; validate accepted file formats; store uploads with the application; display an error on missing/invalid documents." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload ;
    sd:notes "Same real match as 29.2.4 (docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.7" ;
    sd:title "Field-level and application-level validation for additional endorsement" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform field-level and application-level validations for additional endorsement applications, so that errors are identified before submission." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Field-level validation on entry; application-level validation before submission; failed validations block submission with errors; Teacher- and School-Administrator-specific validations applied; outcomes logged." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.8" ;
    sd:title "Verify MTTC scores for Teacher endorsements" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must perform MTTC score verification for the specific endorsement(s) requested for Teacher certificates, so that eligibility requirements are met." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Validate MTTC scores for Teacher endorsements requiring them; display an error/warning if requirements aren't met; block submission when unmet; save verification results in the application record; log verification checks." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation, cred:AssessmentResultAggregate ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.9" ;
    sd:title "Collect and process required endorsement fees" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must facilitate the collection of required application fees for additional endorsement requests, so that the application can be processed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display the required fee amount; provide a 'Pay Fee' link to CEPAS; set status to 'Pending Payment' if not paid immediately; on successful payment, update status to 'Submitted' (or next workflow step)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PaymentRequirement, cred:AppState_PendingPayment, cred:AppState_Submitted ;
    sd:notes "'Pending Payment' and 'Submitted' status names are an exact match to cred:AppState_PendingPayment/AppState_Submitted." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_10 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.10" ;
    sd:title "Submit additional endorsement application" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to submit my additional endorsement application, so that the application record is created and I can proceed to payment (if applicable)." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Block submission only for incomplete required fields/uploads/eligibility validations (MTTC/PKS); create an endorsement application record on submission; generate confirmation/payment-link alerts; make submitted data read-only for the educator; display confirmation with a payment-completion option/link." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_SubmitEndorsementAddition ;
    sd:notes "Second mention of 'PKS' in this FDD (alongside 29.1.2) as a named test type distinct from MTTC — see Question_PksAssessmentTypeUnconfirmed." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_3_11 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.3.11" ;
    sd:title "Route endorsement application" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must route the completed endorsement application to the appropriate staff worklist, so that the review process can begin." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Route per endorsement type and Business Rule Management routing rules; 'Routing considers applicable PPR workflows where required (if in future scope)'; log routing decisions with timestamp and user ID; confirm routing; the routed application appears immediately in the appropriate staff worklist." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering ;
    sd:notes "THE HEDGE: this story's own acceptance criteria ('...where required (if in future scope)') is the one place in all of Feature 29.3 that mentions PPR at all — everywhere else (29.3.1-29.3.10) is silent on it, which is what Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's existing 'Confirmed by FDD 29, Feature 29.3, which consistently omits PPR/Needs-Responses routing language' note relies on. The hedge doesn't contradict that note (PPR routing for endorsements is explicitly framed as NOT current scope, 'if future scope'), but it does mean the exemption Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria documents as settled is understood by the FDD's own authors as a current-state carve-out that may not hold going forward. See Question_EndorsementPprHedgeIn29311." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
    rdfs:comment "cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's own sd:notes cite 'FDD 29, Feature 29.3' as confirming that endorsement-addition applications are exempt from the ProfessionalPracticeStatus=Clear auto-approval criterion, based on Feature 29.3 'consistently omitting PPR/Needs-Responses routing language present in every other application type's feature description.' Verified: true for 29.3.1-29.3.10. But 29.3.11 (Route Endorsement Application) explicitly adds 'Routing considers applicable PPR workflows where required (if in future scope)' — the FDD's own authors flag PPR routing for endorsements as a plausible FUTURE addition, not a settled permanent exemption. Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's exception should probably be understood as 'true today, per this FDD, but explicitly flagged by the same FDD as subject to change' rather than an unconditional, permanent carve-out. Recommend a small addition to Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria's own sd:notes reflecting this nuance next time that file is touched — not changed here, since this review's job is to surface it, not silently edit an existing BusinessRule's settled statement." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria, cred:Req_29_3_11 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
    rdfs:comment "This FDD introduces 'Professional Knowledge and Skills (PKS)' as a second named assessment type alongside MTTC (29.1.2 via comment 2095209523/1225736752 'Added'; 29.3.10 independently). Nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl's AssessmentDefinitionAggregate/AssessmentResultAggregate model, nor asp:AssessmentProviderSystem, names PKS specifically — the assumption that it's simply another configured AssessmentDefinition instance (same as any MTTC subject-area test code) rather than a structurally different kind of assessment (different provider, different scoring model, different validity rules) is plausible but unconfirmed against any source describing PKS's own data shape." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:AssessmentDefinitionAggregate, cred:Req_29_1_2, cred:Req_29_3_10 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 29.4: Certificates - View and Print
#################################################################

cred:Req_29_4_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.1" ;
    sd:title "Select and download one or more approved certificates" ;
    sd:statement "As a citizen user, I want to select and download one or more approved certificates, so that I can save digital copies for my records or print them using my device." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display the user's approved/issued certificates; allow single-certificate selection via a per-row download icon; generate the selected certificate(s) in a downloadable format (PDF) on Download; disable/inform if no approved certificates exist; log downloads with timestamp and user ID." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_PrintCredential, cred:Seq_PrintCertificate, cred:TP_CertificatePdfGeneration ;
    sd:notes "'select ONE OR MORE... download icon within the row' (a per-row, single-select-looking icon in WireframeAddendumA) is slightly at odds with its own 'one or more' framing in the story stem vs. 'allows the selection of a SINGLE certificate' in its own acceptance criteria — an internal inconsistency in the FDD text itself, not a graph gap; Op_PrintCredential's own request shape (credentialId, includeEndorsements) is single-credential-oriented, consistent with the acceptance-criteria (singular) reading." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_4_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.2" ;
    sd:title "Generate downloadable cover letters" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce system, I must generate downloadable cover letters based on defined business rules relevant to the type of certificate applied for, so that the user can obtain accurate documentation." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On 'Download Cover Letter', check for pending certificate applications; generate cover letters per certificate-type business rules if any exist; display a list of generated cover letters; allow downloading a selected one; display 'No Pending Applications' if none exist; log all cover letter generation and download actions." ;
    sd:notes "See Question_CoverLetterStoryContradiction below — this is the single most significant finding of this review pass. No satisfiedBy asserted: not because nothing exists (credentialing-technical-design.ttl's cred:TP_CertificatePdfGeneration already has a 'related, not yet modeled' note pointing at exactly this feature), but because drafting a TechnicalProcess now, from contradictory evidence about whether the feature is even wanted, risks encoding the wrong thing." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "discrepancy" ;
    rdfs:comment "Comment thread on this exact story (1655239543, Punniyamoorthy: 'Beth/Caitlin, dont know if we need this story, as we are not going to generate cover letter and it is going to be part of email' -> 570274720, Dontje: 'Agree' -> 884312815, Sinha: 'Got it') reads as the product owner and vendor team agreeing the standalone downloadable-cover-letter-PDF capability described by 29.4.2 is NOT needed, and that cover-letter content should instead be folded into an email (Alerts & Communications territory) rather than a Credentialing-generated document. Despite that apparent agreement, the visible document was never edited to remove or descope 29.4.2 — its full acceptance criteria survive intact, AND Wireframe1 (the landing page, viewed independently) still shows a live 'Print Cover Letter' button plus a note that cover letters print 'for out-of-state applications' specifically — a scope narrower than 29.4.2's generic 'relevant to the type of certificate applied for' framing, and itself unmentioned in 29.4.2's own acceptance criteria. Three different signals (rejected-in-comments / fully-specified-in-text / narrower-scope-in-wireframe) don't agree with each other. credentialing-technical-design.ttl's existing framing of this as merely 'not enough detail specified yet' undersells the actual state: it isn't just underspecified, it's actively contested whether it should exist as a Credentialing-side document-generation feature at all, and if it does, at what scope. Recommend confirming directly with the product owner before modeling a TechnicalProcess for it." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_4_2 ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_4_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.3" ;
    sd:title "Confirm enrollment with a Michigan EPP" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce Citizen user, I want to confirm my enrollment with a Michigan Educator Preparation Provider (EPP) from my landing page, so that I can establish my enrollment record in the system for verification by my EPP." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Display a 'Confirm Enrollment' action button on the landing page; on click, prompt for EPP Name (from a list of EPPs), Program Level (per EPP), Program Type (per Program Level), and Student ID; on successful submission, automatically send an email to the applicant." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation ;
    sd:notes "PARTIAL match only, and on the wrong side of the write/read line: epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation (per epp-api.ttl) is a READ operation (checking enrollment status), while this story describes a WRITE — the citizen submitting a new enrollment-confirmation record for EPP verification. No write operation for citizen-submitted enrollment confirmation exists in either credentialing-api.ttl or epp-api.ttl. This story itself was a LATE ADDITION to the Addendum's own numbering (see Question_ConfirmEnrollmentLateAddition) — it reuses the 29.4.3 number already claimed by the 'View Enrollment Information' heading immediately above it, which is why 29.4.3/29.4.4 collide throughout the rest of Feature 29.4 (see this file's header note). Wireframe4 (Confirm enrollment form, viewed independently) already existed in the main Business Specifications section and matches this story's fields exactly, despite the review thread implying the story itself was newly drafted — the UI design outpaced its own formal user-story writeup." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "discrepancy" ;
    rdfs:comment "Comment thread 566123317 (Punniyamoorthy: 'Missing user story and wireframe for confirm enrollment as a Citizen/Educator') -> 1837999721 (Doherty relaying Yashi/Sinha: 'Noted. I have added a high-level user story for the Confirm Enrollment flow. I will update the story with more granular details once the wireframe is finalized and attached.') -> 514914922 (Doherty relaying Yashi/Sinha, asking what columns/data points the reviewer wants in the enrollment list) explains the origin of Feature 29.4's duplicate/colliding numbering: a 'high-level' Confirm Enrollment story (Req_29_4_3) was inserted late, reusing the 29.4.3 heading number that the pre-existing 'View Enrollment Information' content already used, without renumbering what followed (which is why a second, unrelated story also ends up numbered 29.4.4, see Req_29_4_4 below). The reviewer's own words ('high-level... will update... once the wireframe is finalized') mean 29.4.3 as written should be read as a placeholder-grade story, not a fully detailed one, even though a matching wireframe (Wireframe4) already existed elsewhere in the document from before this thread." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_4_3 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_4_3b a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.4 (heading: View Enrollment Information)" ;
    sd:title "View enrollment status/details in table format" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to view the status and details of my enrollment information in a clear table format, so that I can review my EPP details." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On 'My Professional Learning' > 'View Enrollment Information', retrieve enrollment data from the Manage EPP source; display Student ID, Provider, Program Level, Program(s), Submitted Date, Status, Enrollment Date, Exit Date exactly as provided by the EPP source; include filter/sort options if designed; log each access." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation ;
    sd:notes "The FDD's own text numbers this story '29.4.4' but it sits directly under the '29.4.3 View Enrollment Information' heading and is conceptually that heading's story — kept here as Req_29_4_3b (not Req_29_4_4) to avoid colliding with the differently-themed View-Pending-Applications story that the FDD ALSO numbers 29.4.4 (Req_29_4_4 below); sd:requirementId preserves the FDD's own literal, colliding number verbatim per this file's header note. 'My Professional Learning' as a containing menu location corroborates the comment-96517507 thread (Punniyamoorthy: 'Professional learning is different from Enrollment Information. Need a separate story for view Professional Learning' -> 'Added'/'This has been changed') — Enrollment Information appears to have been nested under a broader Professional Learning area in response to that comment, consistent with plrn:ProfessionalLearningContext (a stub-only context for Credentialing) being the actual home for a standalone 'View Professional Learning' capability this FDD doesn't itself detail. Read operation exists (epp:EnrollmentStatusOperation); filter/sort ('if designed') is explicitly conditional in the FDD's own text, not asserted as required." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "unconfirmed-assumption" ;
    rdfs:comment "Wireframe9 (Enrollment Information, viewed) shows a 3-row static table and was attached in direct response to an earlier 'wireframe needs to be updated' comment (964068277 -> 1600877324 'working on getting the wireframes' -> 1233352176 'new wireframe has been attached'). But a LATER comment on the same thread's target (1047102331, Punniyamoorthy, 2026-04-27 — six weeks after the wireframe was attached) says 'Still missing the wireframe for the table to list all enrollments,' with no further reply in the extracted comment set. It's unresolved whether Wireframe9 (which does show a 3-row table) was considered adequate after all, superseded by a further update not captured in this docx, or genuinely still felt incomplete by the reviewer (e.g. only shows 3 rows, doesn't visually confirm pagination/scrolling behavior for an educator with many enrollments)." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_4_3b ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_4_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.4 (heading: View Pending Certificate Applications)" ;
    sd:title "View pending certificate applications list" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to view a list of all pending certificate applications with status and submission date details, so that I can track my application progress." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On selecting View List of Pending Certificate Applications, check whether pending applications exist; if so, display Application #/Certificate Type/Submitted On/Status per MiEdWorkforce UI/UX table standards; display an informational message if none exist; log each access." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListApplications ;
    sd:notes "Direct match; near-duplicate of 29.1.3's pending-applications display (same table shape) but framed as its own dedicated list view rather than a landing-page section — consistent with WireframeAddendumE's separate 'My Credentials > Applications' tab. Same '29.4.4' collision as Req_29_4_3b — see this file's header note and Question_ConfirmEnrollmentLateAddition." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_4_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29.4.5" ;
    sd:title "Delete a pending certificate application" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce citizen user, I want to delete a pending certificate application that is still in 'Submitted' status, so that I can remove erroneous applications before they are processed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Select a pending application from the list; check its status; if Submitted, allow deletion via a 'More' (three-dot) menu's Delete option; require confirmation before permanent deletion; if no longer Submitted, prevent deletion with an informational message; log deletes with timestamp, user ID, and application ID; deleted applications cannot be recovered by the citizen." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_DeleteApplication, cred:Seq_DeletePendingApplication, cred:AppState_Submitted ;
    sd:notes "Strong direct match, including the exact Submitted-only gate. WireframeAddendumE (viewed) directly confirms the 'More' three-dot menu -> Delete UX pattern described here." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Business Specifications features never promoted into
# the Addendum's own numbering (see this file's header note)
#################################################################

cred:Req_29_BizSpec_AddCollegeCredits a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Add College Credits')" ;
    sd:title "Add college credits toward certificate requirements" ;
    sd:statement "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Add College Credits on the landing page and provide: Course number, Course Title, Semester Credit hours, Name of the College/University, Date Completed. The system will perform business rule validation when collecting the college credit information." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no CollegeCredit-shaped DomainEntity/ValueObject nor any corresponding ApiOperation/Sequence exists anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl/credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-sequences.ttl. This is one of the three Business-Specifications-only features never given its own Addendum Feature number at all (see Question_AddendumOmitsThreeBizSpecFeatures) — genuine coverage gap, grouped with Add DPPD and Complete SCECH Evaluations below since all three share the same 'wireframed and described, never formalized into a numbered story, never modeled downstream' shape." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_BizSpec_AddDPPD a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Add DPPD')" ;
    sd:title "Add District Provided Professional Development (DPPD) hours" ;
    sd:statement "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Add DPPD on the landing page to add: Professional Development Category, Activity Title, School District, Hours Engaged, Date — with Business Rule validation — and will have the ability to submit additional DPPD form(s) as part of the certificate renewal application." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no DPPD-shaped entity or operation exists anywhere in credentialing's files. Dependencies section's own 'College credit validation and DPPD validation will be defined in Business Rule Management (4)' line is consistent with the validation LOGIC being out of Credentialing's own scope, but the DATA CAPTURE (the form itself, the stored DPPD record) has no home either — that half isn't a Business-Rule-Management concern and does need a Credentialing (or Professional Learning) model somewhere. Grouped with the other two unpromoted Business-Specifications features below." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_BizSpec_ViewProfessionalLearningHoursSummary a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'view PD hours by source and total')" ;
    sd:title "View Professional Development hours earned by source and total" ;
    sd:statement "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will have the ability to view the Professional Development hours they earned by source and total hours: College credits, District uploaded PD and SCECHs, DPPD Earned prior to July 01, 2020, Totals." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy. This is exactly the capability comment thread 96517507 (Punniyamoorthy: 'Professional learning is different from Enrollment Information. Need a separate story for view Professional Learning') asked to have split out as its own story — the replies ('Added'/'This has been changed') suggest something was adjusted, but no distinct 'View Professional Learning [hours]' Feature/story number exists anywhere in the Addendum as written; only the enrollment-information view (Req_29_4_3b) got a 'My Professional Learning' menu placement. Whether a genuinely separate PD-hours-summary story was ever drafted elsewhere (a later revision, or FDD 28 - Professional Learning - Processing, named in this FDD's own Dependencies section) isn't confirmable from this document alone." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

cred:Req_29_BizSpec_CompleteSCECHEvaluations a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "29 (Business Specifications, unnumbered — 'Complete SCECH Evaluations')" ;
    sd:title "View and complete SCECH evaluations for attended programs" ;
    sd:statement "The MiEdWorkforce Citizen user will be able to click on Complete SCECH Evaluations on the landing page to view programs attended that are awaiting evaluation (SCECH Sponsor, SCECH Coordinator, Program Name, Event Date, Evaluation), select a record, and submit the evaluation." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: credentialing-domain.ttl's own header comment already documents that 'proflearning's SCECH endpoint' doesn't exist as a real integration ('Left unresolved on purpose so the ambient SHACL check surfaces it as the real, documented gap it is') — this FDD independently describes a full citizen-facing UI (view-awaiting-evaluation list + submit-evaluation action) for exactly that already-known-missing SCECH surface. Corroborates, rather than newly discovers, the existing gap on credentialing's Dependency to plrn:ProfessionalLearningContext." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "Three real, wireframed, field-level-specified capabilities from this FDD's main Business Specifications section (Add College Credits/Wireframe5, Add DPPD + PD-hours-summary/Wireframe6, Complete SCECH Evaluations) were never assigned their own Feature/story number in the Addendum at all — the Addendum only elaborates the landing page (29.1), the generic application flow (29.2), additional endorsements (29.3), and view/print+enrollment (29.4). None of the three has any corresponding DomainEntity, ApiOperation, or Sequence anywhere in credentialing's mied-v3 files either. The SCECH one specifically corroborates an ALREADY-DOCUMENTED gap (credentialing-domain.ttl's own header note on proflearning's missing SCECH endpoint); College Credits and DPPD data-capture are, as far as this review can tell, newly surfaced gaps with no prior corroboration in credentialing-domain.md." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_29_BizSpec_AddCollegeCredits, cred:Req_29_BizSpec_AddDPPD, cred:Req_29_BizSpec_ViewProfessionalLearningHoursSummary, cred:Req_29_BizSpec_CompleteSCECHEvaluations ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .

#################################################################
# Cross-cutting Annotations (feature-level pointers to other Business
# Specifications, per the Dependencies section — same deferral pattern
# as the FDD 11/16 pass's Req_11_6/11_7/16_3)
#################################################################

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:questioning ;
    rdfs:comment "This FDD's own Dependencies section names ten other Business Specifications it relies on (User Authorization (1), role-based dashboard admin (3), Business Rule Management (4) for college-credit/DPPD validation, Alerts and Communications (6), CEPAS (7) for fees, Credential Admin (11) for per-certificate-type configuration, Manage EPP (13) for enrollment data, Educator Certificate - Application Processing (17), Data Collection & Compliance - Employee Assignment Details (22), Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25), Professional Learning - Processing (28)). Of these, this review confirms real mied-v3 conversions exist for: iam (User Authorization), payments (CEPAS/fees), communications (Alerts), epp (Manage EPP), proflearning (Professional Learning Processing). No mied-v3 conversion exists (11 real domains only) for: role-based-dashboard admin (3, dash: stub only), Business Rule Management (4), Credential Admin (11) as a distinct configuration surface beyond what credentialing-domain.ttl's own CredentialDefinition/EndorsementDefinition/AssessmentDefinition aggregates already model, 'Educator Certificate - Application Processing' (17) as a distinct FDD from this one, Employee Assignment Details (22), Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25, though epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData exists as a related but not identical concept). Not modeled as Requirements here per CONVENTIONS.md's 'no possible satisfiedBy/rejection target' rule for whole subject areas outside the 11 converted domains — logged to GAPS.md instead." ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd29Doc .
